// The only case that does not need pos/col declared: at or past
// particle_count the loop makes zero add_particle() calls, so nothing here
// ever runs build_particles() a second time (see particles/gen/add.id's
// note -- build_particles is pos/col's one legal declarer, and its own fill
// touches all 6,000,000 particles, too expensive to pay for twice more).
fill_particles(int particle_index) {
  while (particle_index < (import particle_count)) {
    add_particle(particle_index);
    particle_index = particle_index + 1;
  }
} return void;
(6000000):()
(6000001):()

// pos/col are declared only by build_particles(), whose own fill touches
// every one of (import particle_count)'s 6,000,000 particles -- a real cost
// (confirmed against the actual build: a few seconds, not the 10s case
// cap), paid once here by every case elsewhere in this tree that needs pos
// or col populated, rather than duplicated per check.
particle_state() {
  string state_text = (import particle_positions)[0] + "," + len((import particle_positions)) + "," + (import particle_colors)[0] + "," + len((import particle_colors));
} return string state_text;
